{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Bound sheaves.</b> As the Targum renders: מְאַסְּרִין אֱסָרִין — bound bundles; and so ״נֹשֵׂא אֲלֻמֹּתָיו״ (Psalms 126), and similarly in the language of the Mishnah: וְהָאֲלֻמּוֹת נוֹטֵל וּמַכְרִיז." "<b>My sheaf arose.</b> It stood upright." "<b>And also stood.</b> Stood upright upon its stand — in upright position."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:02:22.565845671Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}